From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:57:42 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: phy: qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater: add the HS slew
 rate tuning

The repeater has a register for the high-speed transmit slew rate
(TUNE_USB2_SLEW) next to the ones that already have a property. Boards
tune it as they tune amplitude and pre-emphasis.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater.yaml   | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater.yaml
index f29fc335f3f5..7d6c9546b649 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/phy/qcom,snps-eusb2-repeater.yaml
@@ -60,6 +60,12 @@ properties:
     minimum: 0
     maximum: 7
 
+  qcom,tune-usb2-slew:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint8
+    description: High-Speed TX slew rate tuning
+    minimum: 0
+    maximum: 7
+
   qcom,squelch-detector-bp:
     description:
       This adjusts the voltage level for the threshold used to detect valid
-- 
2.43.0

